---
title: Spicy sausage and mushroom pizza
servings: 24
yield: 24 pieces
tags: [italian, pork, make-ahead]
cuisine: italian
time: 1 hour
source: Our own
---

> The time leaves out the dough's cold rest, which is at least a day.

== Dough ==

Pour the @water{880%g}(warm) into a #6-quart container{}, add the
@instant yeast{15%g} and swirl. Add the @flour{1200%g} and mix by hand until no
dry flour is left.

Sprinkle on the @kosher salt{10%g} and mix until it disappears. Cover and leave
at room temperature ~{90%minutes}, until doubled.

Refrigerate at least ~{24%hours} and up to ~{7%days}.

== Toppings ==

Brown the @Italian sausage{1%lb} in a #skillet{} until crisp. Lift it out with a
slotted spoon, leaving 1 tbsp of the fat in the pan.

Cook the @mushrooms{1%lb}(sliced) in that fat until soft, browned and dry.

== Pizza ==

Heat the oven to 500°F. Spread the @olive oil{3%tbsp} over a #half sheet pan{}
and stretch the dough to fill it.

Spread the @crushed tomatoes{6-8%oz} over the dough, sprinkle with the
@red pepper flakes{2%tbsp}, then cover with the @mozzarella{1%lb}. Scatter the
sausage over the cheese and the mushrooms over that.

Bake ~{28%minutes}. Cool on a #wire rack{} ~{3-4%minutes}, then cut into
squares.
